# Kp=K, Ki=K/Ti, Kd=K*Td
# Thesis WingLoop scenario v1_k1: Kp = 7, Ki = 30 1/s, Kd = 8 s. The ASWING control law maps the
# pitch error to F2 in the same angle unit (deg/deg = rad/rad), so these are the gains as written
# (the WingLoop backends use the same gains in deg/rad, i.e. x 180/pi). wingloop_testrun.make_con
# uses this file as a template and writes 00_Pitch_PID_<scenario>.con with each scenario's gains.
# Pitch proportional (P controller)
   2  8  0  -1           ! -1.0 Delta(2) is elevator,  KUELEV = 8 is Theta index
   1  1                   ! only one gain value will be used
   0.0                    ! par1 value doesn't matter for unscheduled gain
   0.0                    ! par2 value doesn't matter for unscheduled gain
   7                   ! gain value Kp
#

# Pitch Integral (I controller)
   2  14  0  -1           ! -0.01 Delta(2) is elevator,  KUELDT = 14 is Int(Theta-Theta_commanded)dt index
   1  1                   ! only one gain value will be used
   0.0                    ! par1 value doesn't matter for unscheduled gain
   0.0                    ! par2 value doesn't matter for unscheduled gain
   30                   ! gain value Ki

# Pitch Derivative (D controller)
   2  5  0  -1           ! -1 Delta(2) is elevator,  KUROTY =  5 is Wy (since the other two euler angles are zero, this is theta_dot) (4 and 6 are for omega_x and omega_z).
   1  1                   ! only one gain value will be used
   0.0                    ! par1 value doesn't matter for unscheduled gain
   0.0                    ! par2 value doesn't matter for unscheduled gain
   8                   ! gain value Kd
#

